wgl/virgl: make OpenGL frames reach the window

Applies to max8rr8/mesa@viogpu_win (62f1e49). Without it, OpenGL renders on the GPU but nothing is shown:

- The DXGI swapchain framebuffer created its D3D11 device with D3D11_CREATE_DEVICE_DEBUG, which fails unless the
  optional Graphics Tools (d3d11sdklayers.dll) are installed, so there was never a swapchain. Create the device
  without it, up front (a failure now falls back to the GDI path), build the swapchain from the device's factory,
  and only ask for tearing when DXGI supports it.
- Create that device on the adapter the window's DC belongs to (the one the virgl screen opened). In an RDP session
  DXGI lists the GPU twice with different LUIDs, and the default adapter's shared textures can't be opened by
  virgl, so every frame was dropped.
- The GDI path (pixel formats with PFD_SUPPORT_GDI, or the fallback) presented through gdikmt, whose present is a
  stub. Read the frame back and draw it with StretchDIBits instead.
- Log why importing a shared resource fails instead of failing silently.

